WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
The first engine is the Council of Europe.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:07.420
Representing 46 member states, it focuses
strictly on protecting human rights,

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.300
democracy, and the rule of law.

4
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.060
Its crowning achievement in bioethics is
the 1997 Oviedo Convention,

5
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.600
a legally binding instrument designed to
protect human rights against

6
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.800
biomedical overreach. The second engine is
the European Union.

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.340
It provides complementary, binding,
economic, and data regulations for its 27

8
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.940
member states. This is implemented most
notably through the GDPR.

9
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.580
and strict enforceable rules governing
clinical trials.

10
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.560
Europe's strategy relies on a deliberate
overlap.

11
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.560
The Council of Europe draws the uncrossable
moral lines, while the European

12
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.092
Union polices the commercial reality of
the society.
